//! The wire runtime: the "idl codecs" of plan section 5.
//!
//! Code generated by `mantis-idl` and the unified log both encode through this
//! module. Everything here validates at the boundary and fails closed
//! (principles 2 and 6):
//!
//! - integers are fixed-width little-endian;
//! - `f32` must be finite, and NaN or infinity is refused on decode;
//! - `bool` is one byte, exactly 0 or 1;
//! - lists, strings, and byte strings carry a `u16` length that must not exceed
//!   the declared bound, and are stored inline in [`BoundedArray`], so decoding
//!   never allocates and a hostile length can never trigger a large allocation;
//! - strings must be valid UTF-8;
//! - enums and bit sets refuse undefined values;
//! - [`decode_exact`] refuses trailing bytes.
//!
//! [`FuzzSample`] produces structurally valid random values for the
//! structure-aware fuzzer in `mantis-testkit`.

mod bounded;

